rsity","http://www.cam.ac.uk/about-the-university/visiting-the-university"],["Research at Cambridge","http://www.cam.ac.uk/research"],["News","http://www.cam.ac.uk/research/news"],["Features","http://www.cam.ac.uk/research/features"],["Discussion","http://www.cam.ac.uk/research/discussion"],["Spotlight on...","http://www.cam.ac.uk/research/spotlight-on"],["About research at Cambridge","http://www.cam.ac.uk/research/research-at-cambridge"]],"fullText":"Skip to main content\n\nStudy at Cambridge\nAbout the University\nResearch at Cambridge\nQuicklinks\nDepartment of Engineering / Research / Academic Divisions / Mechanics Materials and Design / Research Groups\nDepartment of Engineering\nHome\nAbout us\nUndergraduates\nPostgraduates\nResearch\nCollaboration\nEvents and outreach\nServices\nResearch Groups\nMechanics, Materials and Design\nResearch Groups\nApplied Mechanics\nBiomechanics\nEngineering Design\nMaterials Engineering\nGraduate Studies\nResearch Facilities\nEvents\nContact Us\nApplied Mechanics\n\nThe Applied Mechanics research group contains four subgroups, including Computational Mechanics, Dynamics and Vibration, Transportation, and MEMS.\n\nBiomechanics\n\nThe Biomechanics group conducts research in both bioengineering and biomedical engineering subject areas.\n\nEngineering Design\n\nThe Engineering Design Centre, led by Professor P John Clarkson, undertakes research to create knowledge, understanding, methods and tools to improve the design process.\n\nMaterials Engineering\n\nThe Materials Engineering research group is headed by Professor Norman A. Fleck and contains two subgroups: Micromechanics and Superconductivity.\n\n\n\nIntranet\nContact\n\nEngineering Department\nTrumpington Street\nCambridge CB2 1PZ\nUnited Kingdom (map)\nTel: +44 1223 332600 \n\nInformation provided by: web-editor@eng.cam.ac.uk\n\nPrivacy policy\nCookie policy\n\n \n\nUndergraduate teaching\nGraduate study\nResearch\nCollaboration\nGiving to the Department\nEvents and outreach